{"data": [{"author_id": "2109945464246132736", "created_at": "2026-10-21T22:00:13.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2113027605385347427"], "id": "2113027605385347427", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 2, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "A2A, A2P, MCP and similar protocols are solving important pieces of the agentic puzzle.\n\nBut, why should a business allow an external AI agent to operate directly inside its ecosystem?\n\nTake Amazon, Uber or Airbnb. These aren\u2019t simply APIs waiting to be connected to an agent.", "url": "https://x.com/Turnstac/status/2113027605385347427"}, {"article": {"title": "Wednesday Scraps for October 21 '26"}, "author_id": "2050739942892990465", "created_at": "2026-10-21T21:24:29.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2113018611614839174"], "id": "2113018611614839174", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 126, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "https://t.co/FgDV3PVmFh", "url": "https://x.com/fintwitscraps/status/2113018611614839174"}, {"article": {"title": "Claude Duet cannot trade stocks or move your money. Here is what it can do, and what it costs"}, "author_id": "1563266793900474368", "created_at": "2026-10-21T20:37:34.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2113006805043249551"], "id": "2113006805043249551", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 1, "impression_count": 17, "like_count": 2, "quote_count": 1, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 1}, "text": "https://t.co/WNLUeVbaGh", "url": "https://x.com/klaivor/status/2113006805043249551"}, {"author_id": "1305356667354112000", "created_at": "2026-10-21T20:35:47.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2113006356106301731"], "id": "2113006356106301731", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 117, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "$META \n\nMuse for shopping is a pretty interesting use case. Zuckerberg just told us average ticket in this segment is $200. \n\nAgents spending your money is also bullish for $ETH and in turn $BMNR", "url": "https://x.com/itselijahcheng/status/2113006356106301731"}, {"article": {"title": "anthropic built a coworker that texts you first"}, "author_id": "2092269911754059776", "created_at": "2026-10-21T20:27:50.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2113004352667287889"], "id": "2113004352667287889", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 67, "like_count": 1, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 1, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "an agent that interrupts you 50 times is a spam filter running in reverse https://t.co/zkp2RtnD1B", "url": "https://x.com/DrAi404/status/2113004352667287889"}, {"author_id": "1899021201487310848", "created_at": "2026-10-21T20:12:29.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2113000493601652971"], "id": "2113000493601652971", "in_reply_to_user_id": "1899021201487310848", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 1, "impression_count": 860, "like_count": 5, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2112981247542898867", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "Update:\n\nMeta Muse Wonder is now available on OpenCode \u2014 but it\u2019s not free, it\u2019s paid ($4 per 1M input tokens / $20 per 1M output). Meta\u2019s new 1M-context frontier model built for coding and long agentic tasks.", "url": "https://x.com/zazzy_stardust/status/2113000493601652971"}, {"attachments": {"media_keys": ["3_2112991943193976832"]}, "author_id": "1730565937831538688", "created_at": "2026-10-21T19:38:32.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2112991946306433045"], "id": "2112991946306433045", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 1, "impression_count": 713, "like_count": 7, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 1, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "Walmart ( $WMT ) unveiled Agent Gateway, a platform allowing approved AI agents to search for products and make purchases across Walmart and Sam\u2019s Club, embracing agentic shopping as rival Amazon ( $AMZN ) restricts autonomous purchasing.\n\n\u2022AI integrations:\nBuilt using https://t.co/eGEJiDNxhI", "url": "https://x.com/CaktusJxck/status/2112991946306433045"}, {"author_id": "2076659370994077696", "created_at": "2026-10-21T18:23:27.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2112973053671907762"], "id": "2112973053671907762", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 20, "like_count": 1, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 2}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2112948459745763530", "type": "quoted"}], "text": "The model menu just got wider. OpenCode added Meta Muse Wonder today. That's access through an existing coding workflow\u2014not evidence it'll handle your codebase better. What's your go/no-go test before switching models? https://t.co/ZK00E5RGcs", "url": "https://x.com/AI_N0W/status/2112973053671907762"}, {"author_id": "1755260056491409408", "created_at": "2026-10-21T17:12:04.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2112955089942102365"], "id": "2112955089942102365", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 107, "like_count": 3, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2112948459745763530", "type": "quoted"}], "text": "meta muse wonder is now available on opencode \ud83d\udc40\n\nanother model to try for your coding workflow \n\nLfg \ud83d\udd25 https://t.co/5cuf7LVwSy", "url": "https://x.com/Sudhanicn0/status/2112955089942102365"}, {"author_id": "1958606814280654849", "created_at": "2026-10-21T17:00:35.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2112952199571497223"], "id": "2112952199571497223", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 19, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 1, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "Meta Muse just hit 10.9M downloads in 40 days \u2014 beating ChatGPT on the App Store.\n\nThe race isn't just about models anymore. It's about who owns the agent layer.\n\nMeta built the distribution. Now they're building the brain. \ud83d\udc40 #AI", "url": "https://x.com/r0bin_yz/status/2112952199571497223"}, {"author_id": "13348", "created_at": "2026-10-21T16:54:53.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2112950156379512896", "2112950764348014878"], "id": "2112950764348014878", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 250, "impression_count": 7339350, "like_count": 308, "quote_count": 8, "reply_count": 62, "retweet_count": 25}, "text": "I've been GrokBot pilled.\n\nFirst of all, Grok knows me better than other bots, like Meta Muse, thanks to the 300,000 posts I've done here for 20 years. \n\nBut now that GrokBot @bot can read lists, it opens up powerful new personalized news capabilities. \n\nI've done this for about", "url": "https://x.com/Scobleizer/status/2112950764348014878"}, {"author_id": "13348", "created_at": "2026-10-21T16:52:28.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2112950156379512896", "2112950764348014878"], "id": "2112950156379512896", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 1, "impression_count": 1780, "like_count": 2, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "I've been GrokBot pilled.\n\nFirst of all, Grok knows me better than other bots, like Meta Muse, thanks to the 300,000 posts I've done here for 20 years. \n\nBut now that GrokBot @bot can read lists, it opens up powerful new personalized news capabilities. \n\nI've done this for about", "url": "https://x.com/Scobleizer/status/2112950156379512896"}, {"author_id": "2891280648", "created_at": "2026-10-21T16:44:58.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2112948269261185470"], "id": "2112948269261185470", "in_reply_to_user_id": "2071348070760013824", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 12, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2112898195810390181", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@nvandewetering I connected Meta Muse to GitHub (it was kind of a pain), and now I have it working on different repos\n\nOnly problem is that it's not fast at all. Very much an \"add a new feature and run automated tests while I sleep\" kind of thing", "url": "https://x.com/midnightbobarun/status/2112948269261185470"}, {"article": {"title": "Stop renting your memory to AI apps"}, "author_id": "2171647674", "created_at": "2026-10-21T16:30:16.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2112944567926554801"], "id": "2112944567926554801", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 1, "impression_count": 280, "like_count": 2, "quote_count": 2, "reply_count": 1, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "https://t.co/KsvOh0e2hY", "url": "https://x.com/rav4nn/status/2112944567926554801"}, {"article": {"title": "Monid Launches an Agent-Native Commerce Channel with InFlow"}, "author_id": "1993023200738131968", "created_at": "2026-10-21T15:59:08.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2112936733251924057"], "id": "2112936733251924057", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 3, "impression_count": 327, "like_count": 6, "quote_count": 1, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 1}, "text": "https://t.co/e4IfdkAnQr", "url": "https://x.com/inflowpayai/status/2112936733251924057"}, {"author_id": "1662868113782612054", "created_at": "2026-10-21T15:49:47.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2112934378997223873"], "id": "2112934378997223873", "in_reply_to_user_id": "1662868113782612054", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 3, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2112933837814571104", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "Sources (sizes only, not per-core speed; checked Oct 20, 2026):\nGrok Bot: measured on my account, Oct 20, 2026 (xAI publishes no spec).\nOpenAI dots (user-measured): https://t.co/rhodtQl1bC and https://t.co/ScisXZLPiN\nManus Advanced (official): https://t.co/A6aOttT7Gu\nMeta Muse", "url": "https://x.com/JerryWLambert/status/2112934378997223873"}, {"attachments": {"media_keys": ["3_2112916858454310912"]}, "author_id": "1682508485668241408